T-005 RED re-derivation, captured 2026-08-25 against the current tree (HEAD 3bc2368a).

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------
The four archived RED logs in this directory (red-sh.log, red-ps1.log, red-bash.log,
red-powershell.log) each report 54 passed / 4 failed with "TEST-009.2: assert_terminal
remains byte-identical" PASSING. That tally cannot be produced by the test file this
repository now ships. tests/loop-inventory.tests.sh:408 pins
EXPECTED_TERMINAL_SHA=f325a4df4a276cf4a4bc7a4051032693cceb6bff6db99fce27eb4b13b18473df,
the hash of the POST-7652d01b assert_terminal body -- the one containing the
`_loop_trace_emit done-transition done-transition:assert-terminal` call. A RED
reconstruction in which _loop_trace_emit does not exist cannot contain that call, so
TEST-009.2 must FAIL there. The archived logs were captured against the previous test
file, which pinned the old baseline cc07ecf6216b77b4b33b3b5f12534868a314f669165540b8accd0fdfc10a2367.
They are evidence for a superseded pair. That generation is gone -- it is not
reconstructed here, and nothing below should be read as restoring it.

Two differentials are re-derived instead, both by `git archive HEAD` into a scratch tree
with only the driver/registry files replaced from an older commit, keeping the CURRENT
tests.

RED-A -- current tests vs 45dda57f^ (T-005's own pre-task baseline)
RED-B -- current tests vs 7652d01b^ (T-005 present; producer NOT yet wired into
         assert_terminal). This is the differential for the 2026-08-21 change, which had
         no failing-first capture of any kind.

LIMITATION, STATED PLAINLY
--------------------------
Both are reconstructions taken after the code existed, not failing-first captures. RED-B
in particular proves only that TEST-009.2's re-baselined hash rejects the pre-change
body: it is a non-vacuity proof for the lock, not evidence that the producer call was
driven test-first. No test in this suite asserts that the done-transition event
originates inside assert_terminal rather than from a caller, so no reconstruction
available here can supply that.

